WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
(audience cheering)
- Good evening.

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.400
Good evening, good evening.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.150
Oh, Angela. (clicks tongue)

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.790
Tonight I have the honor of presenting

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:15.550
an Academy Award to a national treasure,

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:20.550
- [Attendee] Yeah!
(audience cheering)

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.610
- The incomparable Angela Bassett,

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.133
in case you all didn't know.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.197
I was blessed to work with
Angela in two beloved films,

00:00:32.197 --> 00:00:34.620
"How Stella Got Her Groove Back"

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.584
and "Boyz n the Hood".

00:00:36.584 --> 00:00:40.140
(audience clapping)

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.880
In "How Stella Got Her Groove Back"

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.950
Angela played the title role,

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.510
and I played her younger sister,

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:48.540
which was the easiest role I could imagine

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:52.560
because Angela really is a sister to me.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.393
Truly.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:57.210
My sister and I first crossed paths

00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:00.184
on a little show called "227". (laughs)

00:01:00.184 --> 00:01:01.620
(audience cheering)

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:02.610
You didn't know I was gonna bring

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.760
that one out on you, right? (laughs)

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.330
Only to later have our coming
out party in the same film,

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.834
John Singleton's "Boyz n the Hood".

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:14.790
(audience clapping)

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:18.180
Now, it's not often you
get to cut your teeth

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:21.990
in a history-making modern
classic, but we did.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.540
And "Boyz n the Hood" is still studied

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.390
and celebrated today for many reasons.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:30.330
But right at the top
is Angela's performance

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:33.540
as the unforgettable mother
fighting for her son,

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.242
the iconic Reva Styles.

00:01:36.242 --> 00:01:37.590
(audience clapping)

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.590
Now, little did Angela know

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:43.320
that Reva Styles would send her on a path

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:46.620
to embody some of the
most significant women

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.630
of the civil right movement,

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:52.260
and become one of the
most in-demand actresses

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.420
of the next 30 years.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.610
On screens big and small,

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:00.117
she has mesmerized us in over 100 roles.

00:02:01.741 --> 00:02:05.010
(audience clapping)

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:09.870
But it's the quality, not the quantity

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:12.870
of her performances
that sets Angela apart.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:16.440
I mean, let's talk about range, okay?

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:20.732
Who else could play Betty Shabazz twice?

00:02:20.732 --> 00:02:21.660
(audience laughs)

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:26.340
Go on to playing a vampire,
then go from playing Rosa Parks

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:29.460
to a sports reporter,
and Coretta Scott King

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.301
to playing the Secret Service Director?

00:02:32.301 --> 00:02:35.850
(laughs) I mean, not only did
she run the Secret Service,

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:38.910
she was a CIA director, a U.S. attorney,

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:42.240
a top official at 1600
Pennsylvania Avenue,

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.451
and an animated Michelle Obama.

00:02:44.451 --> 00:02:45.420
(audience clapping)
(audience laughing)

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.540
Okay, that leads me to
ask you something, Angela.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:50.100
With all that experience,

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.901
why aren't you running for president?

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:52.734
(audience laughing)

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:54.390
I'm down with it.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:58.380
I mean, wait a minute.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.493
Let's not forget her Tina Turner.

00:03:01.493 --> 00:03:06.493
(audience cheering)
(audience clapping)

00:03:07.002 --> 00:03:10.680
I revisit that film annually

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.980
and her performance still blows me away.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.603
Okay, fun fact,

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.680
you remember this when
we were in Arrowhead

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:24.680
at our friend's house, you
pulled me up to sing back-up

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:28.590
for an impromptu karaoke session.

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.821
For a quick moment, I felt like an Ikette.

00:03:30.821 --> 00:03:33.210
(audience laughing)

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:38.210
Man, bottom line, Angela has
lived a career for the ages,

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.820
and I swear she is ageless.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.720
Truly beyond.
(audience clapping)

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:48.240
Angela's talent is something that everyone

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.120
who has worked with her
will share with you,

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:56.120
work with Angela on set and
you become her friend for life.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:59.220
She has stitched a sisterhood that exists

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:04.220
simply because of who she is
as a woman and a human being.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.360
And so many times I've heard people say

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:10.860
that Angela is the very
embodiment of Black excellence.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:12.870
But let me correct that.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:16.050
She has a perspective and a voice

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:20.190
and a beauty that is proudly Black.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:22.920
But what she embodies at her core

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:25.173
is beyond anything that is skin-deep.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:30.668
She is artistic excellence
embodied in human form.

00:04:30.668 --> 00:04:31.889
(audience clapping)
(audience cheering)

00:04:31.889 --> 00:04:36.806
(triumphant music)

